## Exercise 7: Check Prime Number
**Problem:** Write a program to check whether a number is prime using a `for` loop.

### Solution:
```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int n, i, flag = 1;
    printf("Enter a number: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);
    for(i = 2; i <= n/2; i++) {
        if(n % i == 0) {
            flag = 0;
            break;
        }
    }
    if(n > 1 && flag)
        printf("%d is a prime number.\n", n);
    else
        printf("%d is not a prime number.\n", n);
    return 0;
}
```
**Explanation:** The loop checks divisibility up to `n/2`, breaking early if a factor is found.

